{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>ישליו</b> — for it appears that they are the robbers who commit violence publicly, in tranquility." "<b>וישליו</b> — he uses it for himself, and afterwards for another with him, like \"יחי ראובן ואל ימות\" (Deuteronomy 33:6), whose sense is \"and let not his מתי be,\" מתי in the sense of \"ואני מתי מספר\" (Job 7:3)." "<b>בטוחות</b> — its sense is secure dwellings, from בטח." "<b>לאשר הביא אלוה בידו</b> — worshippers of idols, who make their god by their hand. [n: כו״ם resolved as the standard abbreviation for כוכבים ומזלות (celestial bodies and constellates).]"], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:32.303498923Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}